@6137 = ~Shield Mind and Body~

@6138 = ~Shield Mind~

@6139 = ~Shield Body~

@6140 = ~Shield Mind and Body
(Abjuration)

Level: 7
Range: 0
Duration: 2 turns
Casting Time: 7
Area of Effect: The caster
Saving Throw: None

Upon casting, the spell envelops the caster in two distinct layers of shielding energy.
The Shield Body layer fortifies the caster’s physical form, granting immunity to poisons, blindness, and deafness, while also clearing the air that the caster inhales, protecting from poisonous and acidic cloud effects.
The Shield Mind layer grants mental clarity and protects from all forms of fear, sleep, berserk, mind control and any similar effects.~

@6141 = ~Ray of Fragmentation (Evocation)
Level: 4
Range: Visual range of the caster
Duration: Instantaneous
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: Special
Saving Throw: None

Once cast on a golem, this powerful spell will penetrate the creature's magic resistance and will inflict inerrable damage. The spell will also affect up to 2 other golems standing nearby. The amount of damage depends on the golem type according the following table:

- Flesh, Stone, Clay, Sand and Iron golems: 4D8
- Coin, Gem, Amber, Brain and Adamantite golems: 2D8
- Ice and Elemental golems: 1D8

Other types of golems cannot be affected by the spell and will take no damage.~

@6142 = ~Poison
(Necromancy)

Level: 4
Range: 15 ft.
Duration: 1 turn
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: 1 creature
Saving Throw: Special

Through this spell, the caster can inject strong poison into the body of his target. The damage inflicted depends on the level of the caster as detailed below:
 7–9th level: 2d8 + 2/round
 10–12th level: 3d8 + 3/round
 13–14th level: 4d8 + 4/round
 15–16th level: 6d8 + 5/round
 17+ level: 8d8 + 6/round
Those who make their Saving Throws against Poison only suffer the initial portion of the damage.~

@6143 = ~Earthquake
(Alteration)

Level: 7
Sphere: Elemental (Earth)
Range: 40 ft.
Duration: Instant
Casting Time: 8
Area of Effect: Special
Saving Throw: Special


When casting this spell, the caster selects 3 points in his range of vision as the epicenters of small yet powerful tremors, each with an 12-foot diameter. All creatures in the area suffer 2d6 crushing damage that bypasses Magic Resistance and drop to the ground for 1 round. A successful Saving Throw vs. Spell negates the fall.

As the caster gains experience, the spell becomes more potent: at level 17, the number of tremor areas increases to 4, and at level 20, it rises to 5.

This spell will affect both enemies and friends of the caster's, so care must be taken in its use. Tremor areas can overlap to increase the damage output to a smaller group of creatures.~

@6144 = ~Blessing of Talos~

@6145 = ~Hand of Undoing (Necromancy)
Level: 7
Range: Touch
Duration: Instantaneous
Casting Time: 7
Area of Effect: One golem
Saving Throw: None

This powerful spell enables the caster to focus his life energy towards a golem and apply a massive shock to the target's internal animating force upon touching it. The spell will inflict considerable damage, which depends on the golem type according the following table:

- Flesh, Stone, Clay, Sand and Iron golems: 8D8 +40
- Ice, Elemental, Coin, Gem, Amber, Brain and Adamantite golems: 4D8 +20
- Greater Elemental, Ultra, Supreme and any other unique powerful golems: 2D8 +10.

Additionally when the mage starts casting this spell, he or she becomes completely invisible to any golem for 4 seconds, which makes this spell easier to cast without interruption.~


@6146 = ~Shield Bash~

@6147 = ~Shield Bash~

